@page "/integration-overview"

<PageTitle>Integration Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / MICROSOFT 365 DIRECTION"
          Title="Integration Overview"
          Subtitle="OperationsFlow is currently local, but the Week 3 evidence system is shaped so the same workflow can move toward Microsoft 365, SharePoint document libraries, Microsoft Graph, Entra ID, Teams/Outlook notifications, and Power BI reporting."
          BadgeText="Integration Ready"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-info">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/prototype-scope">Prototype Scope</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/admin-settings">Admin Settings</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="🔗">
    <p>
        This page explains how the local OperationsFlow workflow maps to a production Microsoft 365 implementation.
        Week 3 proves the local business workflow. Week 4 should replace the provider/authentication layer without redesigning the whole app.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Current Mode"
                Value="Local"
                Detail="SQLite records, local evidence storage, and local Activity Log."
                Icon="💻"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Storage Target"
                Value="SharePoint"
                Detail="Document library storage through Microsoft Graph."
                Icon="☁️"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Auth Target"
                Value="Entra ID"
                Detail="Production login and role-aware access control."
                Icon="🔐"
                Tone="warning" />

    <MetricCard Title="Reporting Target"
                Value="Power BI"
                Detail="Reusable management reporting and evidence coverage review."
                Icon="📊"
                Tone="default" />
</MetricGrid>

<InfoPanel Title="Integration direction"
           Subtitle="The Week 3 local system now maps cleanly to a Microsoft 365 production implementation."
           Tone="default">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Records</span>
            <h3>Workflow data</h3>
            <p>
                Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Risk, Training, and supporting modules currently run locally through the app database.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Evidence</span>
            <h3>SharePoint-ready files</h3>
            <p>
                Attachments are already linked through metadata and a storage service shape, making SharePoint a provider swap instead of a page rebuild.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Identity</span>
            <h3>Entra ID path</h3>
            <p>
                Week 4 can add Microsoft Entra ID authentication and map users into Admin, Manager, Reviewer, Worker, and ReadOnly roles.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Automation</span>
            <h3>Teams / Outlook / Power Automate</h3>
            <p>
                Reminders, overdue actions, management review prompts, and document follow-up can move into production notification workflows.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<TableCard Title="Integration map"
           Subtitle="The current local implementation and the Microsoft 365 production target line up cleanly.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>OperationsFlow feature</th>
                <th>Current local implementation</th>
                <th>Microsoft 365 / production target</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Workflow records</span></td>
                <td>SQLite tables and EF Core services</td>
                <td>SQL database, Microsoft Lists, Dataverse, or hybrid integration depending on client size and requirements.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Evidence files</span></td>
                <td>Local provider under wwwroot/uploads</td>
                <td>SharePoint document library via Microsoft Graph.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Attachment metadata</span></td>
                <td>DocumentAttachment rows in SQLite</td>
                <td>Application metadata plus SharePoint drive item ids, web URLs, eTags, and library paths.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Authentication</span></td>
                <td>No enforced local auth</td>
                <td>Microsoft Entra ID authentication.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Roles</span></td>
                <td>Documented readiness model only</td>
                <td>Entra groups, app roles, policy-based authorization, and SharePoint permissions alignment.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Notifications</span></td>
                <td>Local reminders and reports</td>
                <td>Power Automate, Outlook email, Teams alerts, and scheduled review reminders.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Reporting</span></td>
                <td>In-app reports and CSV exports</td>
                <td>Power BI model using app exports, database views, SharePoint/List data, or a reporting dataset.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Audit trail</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log table</td>
                <td>Application audit log plus Microsoft 365 audit/compliance records where available.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="SharePoint / Graph configuration needed"
               Subtitle="Week 4 needs real tenant and app registration details before the provider can be implemented."
               Tone="info">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Tenant id:</strong>
                <span>Connects the app to the correct Microsoft 365 tenant.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Client id:</strong>
                <span>Identifies the app registration used for Microsoft Graph access.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Secret/certificate:</strong>
                <span>Allows secure server-side Graph authentication.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Site id:</strong>
                <span>Points OperationsFlow to the correct SharePoint site.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Drive/library id:</strong>
                <span>Controls where evidence files are uploaded.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Permission scopes:</strong>
                <span>Controls upload, read, download, and delete/archive behaviour.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Suggested SharePoint folder convention"
               Subtitle="Evidence should stay understandable even when viewed directly in SharePoint."
               Tone="success">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Root:</strong>
                <span>OperationsFlow Evidence</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Work Orders:</strong>
                <span>OperationsFlow Evidence / WorkOrders / WO-1001</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Corrective Actions:</strong>
                <span>OperationsFlow Evidence / CorrectiveActions / CA-1</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Document Intake:</strong>
                <span>OperationsFlow Evidence / DocumentIntake / DI-7</span>
            </li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item">
                <strong>Metadata:</strong>
                <span>Application still stores structured DocumentAttachment records.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<TableCard Title="Week 4 provider behaviour"
           Subtitle="The production provider should match the local workflow but use SharePoint behind the storage service.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Action</th>
                <th>Local behaviour today</th>
                <th>SharePoint behaviour in Week 4</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Upload</span></td>
                <td>Save file to wwwroot/uploads and create metadata row.</td>
                <td>Upload file to SharePoint drive/library folder and store drive item metadata.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Open/download</span></td>
                <td>Open local static file path.</td>
                <td>Use Graph download URL, SharePoint web URL, or controlled app download endpoint.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Soft delete</span></td>
                <td>Mark attachment inactive/deleted in metadata and keep traceability.</td>
                <td>Mark attachment inactive and either archive, recycle, or retention-handle the SharePoint file.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Audit</span></td>
                <td>Write Activity Log entry.</td>
                <td>Write app Activity Log entry and rely on Microsoft 365 audit/compliance where configured.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Permissions</span></td>
                <td>No enforced production auth.</td>
                <td>Enforce Entra ID role policy and align SharePoint access with application permissions.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<GuidanceNote Title="Integration rule" Icon="✅" Tone="info">
    <p>
        Week 4 should not rebuild Work Orders, Corrective Actions, Document Intake, Document Library, Data Quality, Reports, or Activity Log.
        The production implementation should keep the same workflow shape and replace the provider/authentication layer underneath it.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>